      "finding": "S4-DR-R1-003",
      "status": "REWORK_COMPLETE_PENDING_INDEPENDENT_FINAL_CLOSURE_VERIFICATION",
      "controller_residual": "OfficialSummaryMethodEvidence.within() checked only n <= N and k <= K, so a group covering every cohort visit with fewer successes than the cohort (or leaving its complement more successes than visits) received criticalGroupsValid=true.",
      "correction": "within() now requires n <= N, k <= K and K - k <= N - n per source stratum: the complement must be able to carry the remaining successes. The refusal uses the existing same-cohort reason SUMMARY_CRITICAL_GROUP_OUTSIDE_TOTAL; the reported group is retained in lineage; source strata and the independent total keep their qualification; overlapping groups remain lawful; no sum-to-total rule was added; no metric, group vocabulary, threshold or approval was created.",
      "scoping": "A contradictory group removes method qualification for that observation's groups only (existing all-or-nothing flag); pathQualified, primaryRatio, sourceStratified and sourceStrataQualified are unchanged, so the primary Outcome remains computable and the affected protection reads UNDETERMINED, never PASS.",
      "positive_counterexamples": [
        "Lawful whole-cohort, empty, zero-slack and overlapping groups qualify at unit and signed-HTTP/isolated-DB level (retained group counts exposed to the formal comparison).",
        "The equivalent DETAIL/SUMMARY 0.634 formal comparison still holds (rerun).",
        "A qualified late SUMMARY fact (source strata + critical group, superseding the original) is enqueued by the existing intake, processed once by RecalculationService.runOnce, produces one LATE_FACT revision with observedDifference 0.49 under the same frozen reference, keeps the original result, the frozen plan and both observations, and a delivery retry republishes nothing."
      ],
      "negative_counterexamples": [
        "Both Controller counterexamples (N=10,K=9: n=10,k=8 and n=9,k=0) are refused at unit level with exactly SUMMARY_CRITICAL_GROUP_OUTSIDE_TOTAL.",
        "Signed normal-role HTTP intake of an 80/7 group inside an 80/8 source stratum keeps pathQualified, primaryRatio 0.1 and sourceStrataQualified=true, sets criticalGroupSourceStrataQualified=false with that reason, and exposes no group counts to the comparison.",
        "Through the formal Outcome journey the same class of group leaves verdict MET, protection UNDETERMINED, CORE state UNQUALIFIED with CRITICAL_GROUP_TARGET_UNQUALIFIED and observedDifference 0.634 intact.",
        "Individual bounds (n > N, k > K), unproven source totals, missing group, missing/expired profile, wrong version, malformed structure, contradiction and caller numbers remain fail-closed (rerun)."
      ]
    },
